{"id":"nave:music","source":"nave","name":"Music","slug":"music","seeAlso":["Trumpet","Cymbal","Harp","Pipe","Psaltery","Timbrel","Praise","Psalms"],"entries":[{"text":"Teachers of 1Ch 15:22; 25:7,8; 2Ch 23:13","refs":[["1Chr",15,22,15,22],["1Chr",25,7,25,7],["1Chr",25,8,25,8],["2Chr",23,13,23,13]]},{"text":"Physical effect of, on man 1Sa 6:15,16","refs":[["1Sam",6,15,6,15],["1Sam",6,16,6,16]]},{"text":"Discoursed during the offering of sacrifices 2Ch 29:27,28","refs":[["2Chr",29,27,29,27],["2Chr",29,28,29,28]]},{"text":"Precentor Ne 12:42","refs":[["Neh",12,42,12,42]]},{"text":"Chief musician Ne 12:42; Hab 3:19","refs":[["Neh",12,42,12,42],["Hab",3,19,3,19]]},{"text":"Chambers for musicians in the temple, in Ezekiel’s vision Eze 40:44","refs":[["Ezek",40,44,40,44]]},{"text":"In heaven Re 5:8,9; 14:2,3; 15:2,3","refs":[["Rev",5,8,5,8],["Rev",5,9,5,9],["Rev",14,2,14,2],["Rev",14,3,14,3],["Rev",15,2,15,2],["Rev",15,3,15,3]]},{"text":"Invented by Jubal Ge 4:21","group":["Instruments Of"],"refs":[["Gen",4,21,4,21]]},{"text":"Invented by David 1Ch 23:5; 2Ch 7:6; 29:26; Am 6:5","group":["Instruments Of"],"refs":[["1Chr",23,5,23,5],["2Chr",7,6,7,6],["2Chr",29,26,29,26],["Amos",6,5,6,5]]},{"text":"Made by Solomon 1Ki 10:12; 2Ch 9:11; Ec 2:8","group":["Instruments Of"],"refs":[["1Kgs",10,12,10,12],["2Chr",9,11,9,11],["Eccl",2,8,2,8]]},{"text":"Made by Tyrians Eze 28:13","group":["Instruments Of"],"refs":[["Ezek",28,13,28,13]]},{"text":"CORNET Da 3:5,7,10","group":["Instruments Of"],"refs":[["Dan",3,5,3,5],["Dan",3,7,3,7],["Dan",3,10,3,10]]},{"text":"DULCIMER, a double pipe Da 3:5,10,15","group":["Instruments Of","Cymbal"],"refs":[["Dan",3,5,3,5],["Dan",3,10,3,10],["Dan",3,15,3,15]]},{"text":"FLUTE Da 3:5,7,10,15","group":["Instruments Of","Cymbal"],"refs":[["Dan",3,5,3,5],["Dan",3,7,3,7],["Dan",3,10,3,10],["Dan",3,15,3,15]]},{"text":"GITTITH, a stringed instrument Ps 8; 81; 84","group":["Instruments Of","Cymbal"],"refs":[["Ps",8,0,8,0],["Ps",81,0,81,0],["Ps",84,0,84,0]]},{"text":"ORGAN, probably composed of pipes furnishing a number of notes Ge 4:21; Job 21:12; 30:31; Ps 150:4","group":["Instruments Of","Harp"],"refs":[["Gen",4,21,4,21],["Job",21,12,21,12],["Job",30,31,30,31],["Ps",150,4,150,4]]},{"text":"SACKBUT, a harp Da 3:5,7,10,15","group":["Instruments Of","Psaltery"],"refs":[["Dan",3,5,3,5],["Dan",3,7,3,7],["Dan",3,10,3,10],["Dan",3,15,3,15]]},{"text":"VIOL, a lyre Isa 5:12; 14:11; Am 5:23; 6:5","group":["Instruments Of","Trumpet"],"refs":[["Isa",5,12,5,12],["Isa",14,11,14,11],["Amos",5,23,5,23],["Amos",6,5,6,5]]},{"text":"(Literally virgins).A musical term which appears in 1Ch 15:20","group":["Alamoth"],"refs":[["1Chr",15,20,15,20]]},{"text":"And in the title of Ps 46:1","group":["Alamoth"],"refs":[["Ps",46,1,46,1]]},{"text":"It appears in the titles of Ps 57:1; 58:1; 59:1; 75:1","group":["Alamoth","(It seems to indicate the rendering of the song by female voices, possibly soprano) -AL-TASCHITH"],"refs":[["Ps",57,1,57,1],["Ps",58,1,58,1],["Ps",59,1,59,1],["Ps",75,1,75,1]]},{"text":"HIGGAION Ps 92:3","refs":[["Ps",92,3,92,3]]},{"text":"(According to Gesenius, it signifies the murmuring tone of a harp, and hence that the music should be rendered in a plaintive manner.) Ps 9:16","refs":[["Ps",9,16,9,16]]},{"text":"(Combined with “Selah,” it may have been intended to indicate a pause in the vocal music while the instruments rendered an interlude.) Ps 19:14","refs":[["Ps",19,14,19,14]]},{"text":"These terms are found in the titles of Ps 53:1; 88:1","group":["Makalath, Maschil, Leannoth"],"refs":[["Ps",53,1,53,1],["Ps",88,1,88,1]]},{"text":"This musical sign occurs in the titles of Ps 32:1; 42:1; 44:1; 45:1; 52:1; 53:1; 54:1; 55:1; 74:1; 78:1; 88:1; 89:1; 142:1","group":["Maschil"],"refs":[["Ps",32,1,32,1],["Ps",42,1,42,1],["Ps",44,1,44,1],["Ps",45,1,45,1],["Ps",52,1,52,1],["Ps",53,1,53,1],["Ps",54,1,54,1],["Ps",55,1,55,1],["Ps",74,1,74,1],["Ps",78,1,78,1],["Ps",88,1,88,1],["Ps",89,1,89,1],["Ps",142,1,142,1]]},{"text":"(The meaning is obscure. But its signification where it occurs elsewhere than in the titles of Psalms is equivalent to the English word “instruction,” or to become wise by instruction; hence, Ps 47:7: “Sing ye praises with understand- ing.”)","group":["Maschil"],"refs":[["Ps",47,7,47,7]]},{"text":"A musical term in the titles of Ps 16:1; 56:1; 57:1; 58:1; 59:1; 60:1","group":["Micahtam"],"refs":[["Ps",16,1,16,1],["Ps",56,1,56,1],["Ps",57,1,57,1],["Ps",58,1,58,1],["Ps",59,1,59,1],["Ps",60,1,60,1]]},{"text":"In the title of Ps 9:1","group":["Muth-Labben"],"refs":[["Ps",9,1,9,1]]},{"text":"Appear in the titles of Ps 4:1; 54:1; 55:1; 61:1; 67:1; Hab 3:19","group":["NEGINAH and NEGINOTH"],"refs":[["Ps",4,1,4,1],["Ps",54,1,54,1],["Ps",55,1,55,1],["Ps",61,1,61,1],["Ps",67,1,67,1],["Hab",3,19,3,19]]},{"text":"Appears in the title of Ps 5:1","group":["NEGINAH and NEGINOTH","(Its use seems to have been to indicate that the song should be accompanied by stringed instruments.) -NEHILOTH"],"refs":[["Ps",5,1,5,1]]},{"text":"In the titles of Ps 6:1; 12:1","group":["Sheminith"],"refs":[["Ps",6,1,6,1],["Ps",12,1,12,1]]},{"text":"In the title of Ps 7:1","group":["Shiggaion"],"refs":[["Ps",7,1,7,1]]},{"text":"And its plural, SHIGIONOTH, in the title of Hab 3:1","group":["Shiggaion"],"refs":[["Hab",3,1,3,1]]},{"text":"In the titles to Ps 45:1; 60:1; 69:1; 80:1","group":["SHOSHANNIM and SHUSHAN-EDUTH"],"refs":[["Ps",45,1,45,1],["Ps",60,1,60,1],["Ps",69,1,69,1],["Ps",80,1,80,1]]},{"text":"UNCLASSIFIED SCRIPTURES RELATING TO Ge 31:27; Ex 15:1,20,21; 21:17-20; Jud 5:1-3; 11:34; 1Sa 18:6,7; 2Sa 19:35; 1Ki 1:40; 1Ch 6:31,32; 15:16-22,24,27,28; 16:4-39,41,42; 22:3,5,6,27,30; 25:1,5,6,7,8; 2Ch 5:12,13; 20:19,21,22,28; 23:13,18; 29:25-28; 31:2; 35:15,25; Ezr 2:64; 3:10,11; Neh 12:24,27-31; Job 21:12; 30:31; Ps 33:1-4; 68:4,25,26,32-35; 81:1-3; 87:7; 92:1-3; 95:1,2; 98:1-8; 104:33; 105:2; 135:1,2,3; 137:1-6; 144:9; 149:1-3,6; 150:1-6; Pr 25:20; Ec 2:8; Isa 5:12; 14:11; 16:10; 23:16; 24:8,9; 30:29,32; Jer 31:4